is recognized as a reliable source of updated medical information, serving as a reference for various health topics and conditions, including hypogonadism. The resource is designed to assist healthcare professionals in making informed clinical decisions by providing access to current medical literature and guidelines.", "VENLAFAXINA:Venlafaxina is a medication that is primarily used as an antidepressant to treat depressive disorders. It functions as a serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor, which means it helps to increase the levels of these neurotransmitters in the brain, thereby improving mood and alleviating symptoms of depression. In some patients, venlafaxina may be associated with hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin. This medication was prescribed to the patient for managing her psychiatric condition, highlighting its role in the treatment of mental health issues.", "RISPERIDONA:Risperidona, conocida en inglés como risperidone, es un antipsicótico de segunda generación que se utiliza en el tratamiento de diversas condiciones psiquiátricas. Este medicamento se asocia frecuentemente con la hiperprolactinemia, lo que implica que puede provocar aumentos significativos en los niveles de prolactina en el organismo.", "MACROPROLACTINA:La macroprolactina es una forma de prolactina que se forma por la unión de la molécula nativa de prolactina a la inmunoglobulina G, causando hiperprolactinemia analítica.", "HYPERPROLACTINEMIA FAMILIAR:", "BUPROPION:Bupropion is a medication that has been approved for the treatment of depression and for aiding smoking cessation. It functions as a norepinephrine and dopamine reuptake inhibitor, which means it helps to increase the levels of these neurotransmitters in the brain. Additionally, bupropion is known to influence appetite regulation and reward mechanisms. Notably, it does not appear to affect prolactin levels, making it a unique option among antidepressants.", "ANTIPSICOTICOS:Antipsychotics, known as \"antipsicóticos\" in Spanish, are medications primarily used to treat psychiatric disorders. They are particularly noted for being the most common pharmacological cause of hyperprolactinemia, especially among first-generation antipsychotics. Additionally, some antipsychotics are associated with the development of the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH).", "AMISULPIRIDA:Amisulpride is another second-generation antipsychotic linked to frequent and marked increases in prolactin levels.", "SINDROME DE CUSHING:Cushing's syndrome is a condition caused by chronic exposure to high levels of cortisol, often due to a pituitary tumor producing ACTH.", "HIPOFISIS:The pituitary gland, also known as the hipofisis, is a small gland situated at the base of the brain. It plays a crucial role in the endocrine system by producing various hormones, one of which is adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). The presence of tumors in the pituitary gland can lead to the overproduction of ACTH, potentially resulting in Cushing's syndrome, a condition characterized by excessive cortisol levels in the body.", "TAYLOR D:Taylor D is an author of a publication discussing antidepressant-induced hyperprolactinemia.", "VILLAR-TAIBO R:Villar-Taibo R is an author of a publication discussing prolactin disorders.", "SIFONTES-DUBON M:Sifontes-Dubon M is an author of a publication discussing prolactin disorders.", "BERNABEU-MORON I:Bernabeu-Moron I is an author of a publication discussing prolactin disorders."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}